IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpcnt-dates`

-- Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT) -- costs agreements: the questions of the client.
--
-- SEAT: the client: the person who retains a law practice (or for whom one is retained), and who makes or is asked to
-- make a costs agreement with it -- typically an injured person or other claimant offered a "no win, no fee"
-- (conditional) costs agreement with an uplift fee. "May I make a costs agreement?", "Is it in a form the Act allows?",
-- "May it be conditional on winning?", "What must it contain?", "By when can I back out?", "Can my lawyer take a share
-- of what I recover?", "Is my agreement void, and what do I pay or get back if it is?", "Will the costs assessor hold
-- me to its rates?", "Can it be set aside?", "Am I in time to seek review?". The law practice gets no seat here; the
-- costs assessor and the reviewer get none: what they would find is asked as a fact ("if the costs assessor is
-- satisfied that ...").
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date, a list of dates, a choice from a list). No question takes
-- a DEONTIC or an EVENT. Two duties with deadlines are regulative rules run inside a question: the cooling-off period
-- (s 318(3)(e), (6)(b)) and the 28 days to apply for review of a s 323 determination (s 352(2)(a)).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: Part 3.3 Division 5 (costs agreements), whole: s 317 (making costs agreements), s 318
-- (conditional costs agreements), s 319 (uplift fees), s 320 (contingency fees prohibited), s 321 (effect), s 322
-- (certain costs agreements void, what is recoverable and repayable), s 323 (setting aside). Around it: s 295
-- (definitions: conditional costs agreement, uplift fee, litigious matter, sophisticated client), s 296 (third party
-- payers), s 306(1)(c), (d) (who is a sophisticated client), s 308 (uplift fee disclosure), s 314 (basis of recovery,
-- used by s 322(2)), s 339 (assessment of complying costs agreements), s 343 (contracting out by a sophisticated
-- client, used by s 317(5)), s 352(2)(a) (time to apply for review of a s 323 determination); s 4 "business day".
-- Out: see NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), reprint REPL007 as in force at 1 August 2025 (the current reprint on
-- 6 November 2026), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/Legal-Profession-Act-2006-NT-current-reprint-REPL007.txt.
-- The Legal Profession Regulations (NT), which prescribe the uplift cap of s 319(4) and the proceedings of s 318(2)(c),
-- are not deposited: both are asked as facts.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Judgments the Act hands to the costs assessor or the reviewer are
-- INPUTS. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE where the text
-- says no in its own words; NOTHING ("NOTHING-kind") where it does not answer.

§ `Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT): costs agreements, the questions of the client`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The parties, the regulative rules and the record of the agreement's facts
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the client`
    `the law practice`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice terminating the conditional costs agreement`
    `recover the uplift fee`
    `apply to a reviewer for review of the s 323 determination`

-- s 318(3)(e) and (6)(b): the client may terminate by written notice during the cooling-off period; if the client does,
-- the law practice "may not recover the uplift fee". Written as a DO with LEST FULFILLED: a notice within the period
-- brings in the prohibition on the law practice; a period that passes without notice leaves the agreement standing and
-- s 318(6) never applies. Time is counted in days from the day the agreement was made.
GIVEN `the days to the last day of the cooling-off period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the cooling-off period` `the days to the last day of the cooling-off period` MEANS
    PARTY `the client`
    DO    `give written notice terminating the conditional costs agreement`
    WITHIN `the days to the last day of the cooling-off period`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the law practice`
        SHANT `recover the uplift fee`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the law practice` BECAUSE "s 318(6)(b): the client terminated within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee"
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- s 352(2)(a)(i): an application for review of a s 323 determination must be made "within 28 days after ... the
-- determination is made", unless the reviewer allows further time. Time is counted in days from the determination.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the time to apply for review of a set-aside determination` MEANS
    PARTY `the client`
    MUST  `apply to a reviewer for review of the s 323 determination`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the client` BECAUSE "s 352(2)(a): not made within 28 days after the s 323 determination; only the reviewer allowing further time can help"

-- How the costs agreement was made (s 317(2), (3)).
DECLARE `How the agreement was made` IS ONE OF
    `a written agreement`
    `an oral agreement evidenced in writing`
    `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct`
    `an oral agreement with nothing in writing`

-- The kind of matter (s 318(2)). "proceedings prescribed by the regulations": the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) are
-- not deposited, so whether the proceedings are prescribed is the client's fact.
DECLARE `The kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `criminal proceedings`
    `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)`
    `proceedings prescribed by the regulations`
    `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim`

-- The facts of one costs agreement between the client and the law practice. Built inside each exported question from
-- plain inputs.
DECLARE `Costs agreement facts` HAS
    `how made`                                   IS A `How the agreement was made`
    `offer says it is an offer`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `offer says it can be accepted in writing or by conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `offer says what conduct is acceptance`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `says costs are not subject to assessment`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `client listed in s 306(1)(c)`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `costs agreed by tender`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment conditional on success`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `kind of matter`                             IS A `The kind of matter`
    `sets out what counts as success`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `in clear plain language`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the client`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has independent advice statement`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `cooling-off business days`                  IS A NUMBER
    `has uplift fee`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift fee includes disbursements`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift basis separately identified`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift estimate specified`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift estimate not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift range of estimates specified`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift major variables explained`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `litigious`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift percentage`                          IS A NUMBER
    `prescribed uplift percentage`               IS A NUMBER
    `calculated by reference to recovery`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `adopts a fixed costs provision`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Definitions (s 295, s 296, s 306(1)(c), (d))
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 295(1) "sophisticated client means a client to whom, because of section 306(1)(c) or (d), disclosure under section
-- 303 or 304(1) is or was not required". s 306(1)(c) lists clients (a law practice or lawyer, a public company, a large
-- proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a
-- large professional partnership, certain joint ventures, a local government council, a minister, department or
-- public authority); s 306(1)(d): "the legal costs or the basis on which they will be calculated have or has been
-- agreed as a result of a tender process".
GIVEN `listed in s 306(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN, `agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 295 -- a sophisticated client` `listed in s 306(1)(c)` `agreed by tender` IF
        `listed in s 306(1)(c)`
    OR  `agreed by tender`

-- s 295(1) "litigious matter means a matter that involves, or is likely to involve, the issue of proceedings in a court
-- or tribunal". The client states it as one fact.

-- s 295(1) "conditional costs agreement means a costs agreement that provides that the payment of some or all of the
-- legal costs is conditional on the successful outcome of the matter ... but does not include a costs agreement to the
-- extent to which section 320(1) applies". An uplift fee ("additional legal costs ... payable ... on the successful
-- outcome") makes payment of part of the costs conditional on success, so an agreement with an uplift fee is taken to
-- be conditional (fork F6).
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 295 -- a conditional costs agreement` a IF
        a's `payment conditional on success`
    OR  a's `has uplift fee`

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the client is sophisticated` a IF
    `s 295 -- a sophisticated client` (a's `client listed in s 306(1)(c)`) (a's `costs agreed by tender`)

-- s 296(1): who I am, in relation to the law practice. A third party payer is a person who is not the client and is
-- under a legal obligation to pay all or part of the client's legal costs (or has paid them under that obligation);
-- an associated third party payer if the obligation is owed to the law practice; non-associated if it is owed only to
-- the client or another person.
DECLARE `Who I am` IS ONE OF
    `a client who retained the law practice`
    `a client for whom another law practice retained the law practice`
    `an associated third party payer`
    `a non-associated third party payer`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `I am the client` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `another law practice retained this one for me` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I must pay some of the client's legal costs` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `that obligation is owed to the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who I am`
`s 296 -- who I am` `I am the client` `another law practice retained this one for me` `I must pay some of the client's legal costs` `that obligation is owed to the law practice` MEANS
    IF `I am the client`
    THEN IF `another law practice retained this one for me`
         THEN `a client for whom another law practice retained the law practice`
         ELSE `a client who retained the law practice`
    ELSE IF `I must pay some of the client's legal costs`
         THEN IF `that obligation is owed to the law practice`
              THEN `an associated third party payer`
              ELSE `a non-associated third party payer`
         ELSE `someone else`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The contraventions of Division 5, provision by provision
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN `the condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the provision` IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`if` `the condition` `then the provision` `the provision` MEANS
    IF `the condition` THEN LIST `the provision` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 317(2) "A costs agreement must be written or evidenced in writing." s 317(3), (4): an agreement made by a written
-- offer accepted in writing or by other conduct; "The offer must clearly specify" the three things (fork F1).
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 317 -- contraventions` a MEANS
    append
        (`if` (a's `how made` EQUALS `an oral agreement with nothing in writing`)
            `then the provision` "s 317(2): the costs agreement is not written or evidenced in writing")
        (`if` (    (a's `how made` EQUALS `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct`)
               AND (NOT (    a's `offer says it is an offer`
                         AND a's `offer says it can be accepted in writing or by conduct`
                         AND a's `offer says what conduct is acceptance`)))
            `then the provision` "s 317(4): the written offer does not clearly specify that it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement, that it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct, and the type of conduct that will constitute acceptance")

-- s 317(5) "Except as provided by section 343, a costs agreement cannot provide that the legal costs to which it relates
-- are not subject to costs assessment under Division 8." s 343: a sophisticated client may contract out of Division 8.
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 317(5) -- contraventions` a MEANS
    `if` (    a's `says costs are not subject to assessment`
          AND (NOT (`the client is sophisticated` a)))
        `then the provision` "s 317(5): the costs agreement provides that the legal costs are not subject to costs assessment, and you are not a sophisticated client who may contract out under s 343"

-- s 318(2) "A conditional costs agreement may relate to any matter, except a matter that involves: (a) criminal
-- proceedings; or (b) proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth); or (c) proceedings prescribed by the
-- regulations." Fork F2: a conditional costs agreement in an excepted matter contravenes s 318.
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `The kind of matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 318(2) -- an excepted matter` `the matter` IF
    NOT (`the matter` EQUALS `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim`)

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `The kind of matter`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 318(2) -- the exception` `the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `criminal proceedings` THEN "s 318(2)(a): a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter that involves criminal proceedings"
    WHEN `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` THEN "s 318(2)(b): a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter that involves proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)"
    WHEN `proceedings prescribed by the regulations` THEN "s 318(2)(c): a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter that involves proceedings prescribed by the regulations"
    OTHERWISE ""

-- s 318(3) "A conditional costs agreement: (a) must set out the circumstances that constitute the successful outcome
-- ...; (c) must be: (i) in writing; and (ii) in clear plain language; and (iii) signed by the client; and (d) must
-- contain a statement that the client has been informed of the client's right to seek independent legal advice before
-- entering into the agreement; and (e) must contain a cooling-off period of not less than 5 clear business days during
-- which the client, by written notice, may terminate the agreement."
-- s 318(5): (3)(c)(iii), (d) and (e) do not apply to a conditional costs agreement made with a sophisticated client.
-- s 318(4) (an agreement between two law practices under s 317(1)(c)) is not the client's agreement and is not asked.
-- "in writing" (fork F3): a written agreement or a written offer accepted; an oral agreement merely evidenced in
-- writing is not "in writing".
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 318 -- contraventions` a MEANS
    IF `s 295 -- a conditional costs agreement` a
    THEN concat (LIST
        (`if` (`s 318(2) -- an excepted matter` (a's `kind of matter`))
            `then the provision` (`s 318(2) -- the exception` (a's `kind of matter`))),
        (`if` (NOT (a's `sets out what counts as success`))
            `then the provision` "s 318(3)(a): it does not set out the circumstances that constitute the successful outcome of the matter"),
        (`if` (NOT (`s 318(3)(c)(i) -- in writing` a))
            `then the provision` "s 318(3)(c)(i): it is not in writing"),
        (`if` (NOT (a's `in clear plain language`))
            `then the provision` "s 318(3)(c)(ii): it is not in clear plain language"),
        (`if` ((NOT (a's `signed by the client`)) AND (NOT (`the client is sophisticated` a)))
            `then the provision` "s 318(3)(c)(iii): it is not signed by you"),
        (`if` ((NOT (a's `has independent advice statement`)) AND (NOT (`the client is sophisticated` a)))
            `then the provision` "s 318(3)(d): it does not state that you were informed of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it"),
        (`if` ((a's `cooling-off business days` LESS THAN 5) AND (NOT (`the client is sophisticated` a)))
            `then the provision` "s 318(3)(e): it does not contain a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days"))
    ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 318(3)(c)(i) -- in writing` a IF
        (a's `how made` EQUALS `a written agreement`)
    OR  (a's `how made` EQUALS `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct`)

-- s 319(1) "A conditional costs agreement may provide for the payment of additional legal costs (excluding
-- disbursements) on the successful outcome". (2) "The basis of calculation of the uplift fee must be separately
-- identified in the agreement." (3) "An estimate of the uplift fee must be specified in the agreement or, if that is
-- not reasonably practicable, a range of estimates of the uplift fee and an explanation of the major variables that
-- will affect the calculation of the uplift fee." (4) "If a conditional costs agreement relates to a litigious matter,
-- the premium must not exceed the percentage prescribed by the regulations of the legal costs (excluding
-- disbursements) otherwise payable." (5) "A law practice must not enter into a costs agreement in contravention of
-- this section." "premium" is read as the uplift fee (finding 2). The prescribed percentage is the client's input.
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 319(3) -- the estimate is given` a IF
        a's `uplift estimate specified`
    OR  (    a's `uplift estimate not reasonably practicable`
         AND a's `uplift range of estimates specified`
         AND a's `uplift major variables explained`)

GIVEN `litigious` IS A BOOLEAN, `the uplift percentage` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 319(4) -- the premium exceeds the cap` `litigious` `the uplift percentage` `the prescribed percentage` IF
        `litigious`
    AND `the uplift percentage` GREATER THAN `the prescribed percentage`

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 319 -- contraventions` a MEANS
    IF a's `has uplift fee`
    THEN concat (LIST
        (`if` (a's `uplift fee includes disbursements`)
            `then the provision` "s 319(1): the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements"),
        (`if` (NOT (a's `uplift basis separately identified`))
            `then the provision` "s 319(2): the basis of calculation of the uplift fee is not separately identified"),
        (`if` (NOT (`s 319(3) -- the estimate is given` a))
            `then the provision` "s 319(3): no estimate of the uplift fee is specified (nor, where an estimate is not reasonably practicable, a range of estimates and an explanation of the major variables)"),
        (`if` (`s 319(4) -- the premium exceeds the cap` (a's `litigious`) (a's `uplift percentage`) (a's `prescribed uplift percentage`))
            `then the provision` "s 319(4): in a litigious matter the uplift fee exceeds the percentage prescribed by the regulations of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable"))
    ELSE EMPTY

-- s 320(1) "A law practice must not enter into a costs agreement under which the amount payable to the law practice,
-- or any part of that amount, is calculated by reference to the amount of any award or settlement or the value of any
-- property that may be recovered in any proceedings to which the agreement relates." (2) "Subsection (1) does not apply
-- to the extent the costs agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision."
GIVEN `calculated by reference to recovery` IS A BOOLEAN, `adopts a fixed costs provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 320 -- prohibited` `calculated by reference to recovery` `adopts a fixed costs provision` IF
        `calculated by reference to recovery`
    AND (NOT `adopts a fixed costs provision`)

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 320 -- contraventions` a MEANS
    `if` (`s 320 -- prohibited` (a's `calculated by reference to recovery`) (a's `adopts a fixed costs provision`))
        `then the provision` "s 320(1): the amount payable is calculated by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered (a contingency fee)"

-- s 322(1) "A costs agreement that contravenes, or is entered into in contravention of, any provision of this Division
-- is void."
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 322(1) -- the provisions contravened` a MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`s 317 -- contraventions` a),
        (`s 317(5) -- contraventions` a),
        (`s 318 -- contraventions` a),
        (`s 319 -- contraventions` a),
        (`s 320 -- contraventions` a))

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 322(1) -- void` a IF
    NOT (null (`s 322(1) -- the provisions contravened` a))

-- s 322(2) to (5): what the law practice may recover under a void costs agreement, and what it must repay.
-- (2) "legal costs under a void costs agreement are recoverable as set out in section 314(b) or (c)" -- with no valid
-- agreement, s 314(c): "the fair and reasonable value of the legal services provided" (an input: the value found on a
-- costs assessment). (3) not "in excess of the amount that the law practice would have been entitled to recover if the
-- costs agreement had not been void"; "must repay any excess amount received". (4) a s 319 contravention: no part of
-- the uplift fee; "must repay the amount received in respect of the uplift fee". (5) a s 320 contravention: "not
-- entitled to recover any amount in respect of the provision of legal services in the matter"; "must repay any amount
-- received in respect of those services". Fork F7: with a s 319 contravention, the s 322(3) cap is the agreement's
-- costs without the uplift fee.
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`,
      `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` IS A NUMBER,
      `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` IS A NUMBER,
      `the fair and reasonable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover` a `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 322(1) -- void` a)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT (null (`s 320 -- contraventions` a))
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF NOT (null (`s 319 -- contraventions` a))
              THEN JUST (min `the fair and reasonable value` `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift`)
              ELSE JUST (min `the fair and reasonable value` (`the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` PLUS `the uplift fee the agreement would have given`))

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`,
      `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` IS A NUMBER,
      `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` IS A NUMBER,
      `the fair and reasonable value` IS A NUMBER,
      `the amount I have paid` IS A NUMBER,
      `the part of it paid as uplift fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 322 -- what the law practice must repay` a `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value` `the amount I have paid` `the part of it paid as uplift fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover` a `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `recoverable` THEN
        IF NOT (null (`s 320 -- contraventions` a))
        THEN JUST `the amount I have paid`
        ELSE IF NOT (null (`s 319 -- contraventions` a))
             THEN JUST (`the part of it paid as uplift fee` PLUS (max 0 ((`the amount I have paid` MINUS `the part of it paid as uplift fee`) MINUS `recoverable`)))
             ELSE JUST (max 0 (`the amount I have paid` MINUS `recoverable`))

-- Builds the record from plain inputs.
GIVEN `how made` IS A `How the agreement was made`,
      `offer says it is an offer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `offer says acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `offer says conduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `excludes assessment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `listed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `tender` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `conditional` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `matter` IS A `The kind of matter`,
      `success set out` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `plain` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `advice statement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `cooling-off` IS A NUMBER,
      `uplift` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uplift disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uplift basis` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uplift estimate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `estimate impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `range` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `variables` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `litigious matter` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uplift pct` IS A NUMBER,
      `prescribed pct` IS A NUMBER,
      `by reference` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `fixed costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Costs agreement facts`
`the agreement` `how made` `offer says it is an offer` `offer says acceptance` `offer says conduct` `excludes assessment` `listed` `tender` `conditional` `matter` `success set out` `plain` `signed` `advice statement` `cooling-off` `uplift` `uplift disbursements` `uplift basis` `uplift estimate` `estimate impracticable` `range` `variables` `litigious matter` `uplift pct` `prescribed pct` `by reference` `fixed costs` MEANS
    `Costs agreement facts` WITH
        `how made`                                   IS `how made`
        `offer says it is an offer`                  IS `offer says it is an offer`
        `offer says it can be accepted in writing or by conduct` IS `offer says acceptance`
        `offer says what conduct is acceptance`      IS `offer says conduct`
        `says costs are not subject to assessment`   IS `excludes assessment`
        `client listed in s 306(1)(c)`               IS `listed`
        `costs agreed by tender`                     IS `tender`
        `payment conditional on success`             IS `conditional`
        `kind of matter`                             IS `matter`
        `sets out what counts as success`            IS `success set out`
        `in clear plain language`                    IS `plain`
        `signed by the client`                       IS `signed`
        `has independent advice statement`           IS `advice statement`
        `cooling-off business days`                  IS `cooling-off`
        `has uplift fee`                             IS `uplift`
        `uplift fee includes disbursements`          IS `uplift disbursements`
        `uplift basis separately identified`         IS `uplift basis`
        `uplift estimate specified`                  IS `uplift estimate`
        `uplift estimate not reasonably practicable` IS `estimate impracticable`
        `uplift range of estimates specified`        IS `range`
        `uplift major variables explained`           IS `variables`
        `litigious`                                  IS `litigious matter`
        `uplift percentage`                          IS `uplift pct`
        `prescribed uplift percentage`               IS `prescribed pct`
        `calculated by reference to recovery`        IS `by reference`
        `adopts a fixed costs provision`             IS `fixed costs`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The client's questions
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Making a costs agreement (s 317)`

-- s 317(1) "A costs agreement may be made: (a) between a client and a law practice retained by the client; or (b)
-- between a client and a law practice retained on behalf of the client by another law practice; or (c) [between two
-- law practices]; or (d) between a law practice and an associated third party payer." The list is not closed with
-- "only": for anyone else the answer is NOTHING (NOTHING-kind).
@export Under s 317(1) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), may I make a costs agreement with this law practice? TRUE if the Act names you as a party who may; NOTHING if s 317(1) does not name you (it does not say you may not).
GIVEN `I am the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the client: the person the law practice is providing legal services to or for?
      `another law practice retained this one for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are the client: was this law practice retained for you by another law practice (for example a barrister briefed by your solicitors)? Answer false if you retained it yourself.
      `I must pay some of the client's legal costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not the client: are you under a legal obligation (by contract, legislation or otherwise) to pay all or part of the client's legal costs?
      `that obligation is owed to the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you must pay some of the client's costs: is that obligation owed to the law practice itself (not only to the client or someone else)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 317(1) -- may I make a costs agreement with this law practice` `I am the client` `another law practice retained this one for me` `I must pay some of the client's legal costs` `that obligation is owed to the law practice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 296 -- who I am` `I am the client` `another law practice retained this one for me` `I must pay some of the client's legal costs` `that obligation is owed to the law practice`
    WHEN `a client who retained the law practice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a client for whom another law practice retained the law practice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an associated third party payer` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 317(2) to (4). FALSE where the text says no: an agreement neither written nor evidenced in writing (s 317(2)); a
-- written offer that does not clearly specify the three things s 317(4) requires (fork F1).
@export Under s 317(2) to (4) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), is my costs agreement made in a form the Act allows (written or evidenced in writing, or a written offer that says what it must and was accepted)?
GIVEN `how it was made` IS A `How the agreement was made` @desc How was your costs agreement made? One of: a written agreement; an oral agreement evidenced in writing; a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct; an oral agreement with nothing in writing.
      `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does the offer clearly say that it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement? Answer true if it was not made by an offer.
      `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does the offer clearly say that it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct? Answer true if it was not made by an offer.
      `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does the offer clearly say what kind of conduct will count as accepting it? Answer true if it was not made by an offer.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `how it was made` `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` MEANS
    null (`s 317 -- contraventions` (`the agreement` `how it was made` `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
    -- every field the s 317 rules do not read is a fixed placeholder

-- s 317(5) and s 343: "a costs agreement cannot provide that the legal costs to which it relates are not subject to
-- costs assessment" (the text's no), "Except as provided by section 343" (a sophisticated client "may contract out of
-- this Division").
@export Under s 317(5) and s 343 of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), may my costs agreement provide that my legal costs are not subject to costs assessment? TRUE only for a sophisticated client (s 306(1)(c) or (d)); otherwise FALSE, and such a term makes the agreement void (s 322(1)).
GIVEN `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the clients listed in s 306(1)(c): a law practice or Australian legal practitioner; a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company or its subsidiary, or a registered Australian body; a financial services licensee; a liquidator, administrator or receiver; a professional partnership of more than 20 members; certain joint ventures; a local government council; or a minister, government department or public authority? An individual claimant answers false.
      `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the legal costs, or the basis on which they will be calculated, agreed as a result of a tender process?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 317(5) and s 343 -- may my costs agreement take my costs outside costs assessment` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` MEANS
    `s 295 -- a sophisticated client` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process`

§§ `No win, no fee: conditional costs agreements (s 318)`

-- s 318(2): "may relate to any matter, except ..." -- an exception in the text's own words: FALSE.
@export Under s 318(2) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), may my costs agreement make payment of my legal costs conditional on a successful outcome ("no win, no fee")? FALSE for criminal proceedings, Family Law Act proceedings and proceedings prescribed by the regulations; TRUE for any other matter.
GIVEN `the kind of matter` IS A `The kind of matter` @desc What kind of matter is it? One of: criminal proceedings; proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth); proceedings prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) for s 318(2)(c); any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 318(2) -- may my costs agreement be conditional on success` `the kind of matter` MEANS
    NOT (`s 318(2) -- an excepted matter` `the kind of matter`)

-- s 318(3) to (5): what a conditional costs agreement must be and contain. The answer is the list of requirements it
-- does not meet; an empty list means it meets all of them.
@export Under s 318(2) to (5) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), which requirements for a conditional ("no win, no fee") costs agreement does my agreement fail to meet? An empty list means none. Any failure makes the agreement void (s 322(1)).
GIVEN `the kind of matter` IS A `The kind of matter` @desc What kind of matter is it? One of: criminal proceedings; proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth); proceedings prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) for s 318(2)(c); any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim.
      `how it was made` IS A `How the agreement was made` @desc How was your costs agreement made? One of: a written agreement; an oral agreement evidenced in writing; a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct; an oral agreement with nothing in writing.
      `it sets out what counts as success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement set out the circumstances that count as a successful outcome of your matter?
      `it is in clear plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement in clear plain language?
      `I signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sign the agreement?
      `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement contain a statement that you were informed of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it?
      `the cooling-off period in clear business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear business days does the agreement give you to end it by written notice (its cooling-off period)? 0 if it gives none.
      `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the clients listed in s 306(1)(c) (a lawyer or law practice, a public or large company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a large professional partnership, certain joint ventures, a council, a minister, department or public authority)? An individual claimant answers false.
      `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the legal costs, or the basis on which they will be calculated, agreed as a result of a tender process?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` `the kind of matter` `how it was made` `it sets out what counts as success` `it is in clear plain language` `I signed it` `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` MEANS
    `s 318 -- contraventions` (`the agreement` `how it was made` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` TRUE `the kind of matter` `it sets out what counts as success` `it is in clear plain language` `I signed it` `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
    -- every field the s 318 rules do not read is a fixed placeholder

-- s 318(3)(e): the last day of the cooling-off period. The period runs from the day the agreement was made (fork F4),
-- that day not counted, and is the number of clear business days the agreement gives. NOTHING where the agreement gives
-- no cooling-off period (it then fails s 318(3)(e), unless you are a sophisticated client).
@export Under s 318(3)(e) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), what is the last day on which I can end my conditional costs agreement by written notice (its cooling-off period)?
GIVEN `the day the agreement was made` IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into the conditional costs agreement (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-11-06).
      `the cooling-off period in clear business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear business days does the agreement give you to end it by written notice? The Act requires at least 5. 0 if it gives none.
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The public holidays in the Northern Territory in the weeks after the agreement was made (ISO 8601 dates). Saturdays and Sundays are excluded already.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` `the day the agreement was made` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `the public holidays` MEANS
    IF `the cooling-off period in clear business days` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the business day` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `after` `the day the agreement was made` `given the public holidays` `the public holidays`)

DECLARE `Cooling-off answer` IS ONE OF
    `No: you ended the agreement within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee (s 318(6)(b))`
    `s 318(6) does not apply: your notice came after the cooling-off period ended (the text's no)`
    `s 318(6) does not apply: the agreement gives no cooling-off period (it fails s 318(3)(e) unless you are a sophisticated client)`
    `s 318(6) does not apply: the notice is dated before the agreement was made`

-- s 318(6)(b): run as the regulative rule `the cooling-off period`: the client's written notice on the given day, then
-- the law practice seeking the uplift fee on the same day. A breach by the law practice means the uplift fee is barred.
@export Under s 318(6)(b) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), if I end my conditional costs agreement by written notice on a given day, can the law practice still charge me the uplift fee?
GIVEN `the day the agreement was made` IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into the conditional costs agreement (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-11-06).
      `the cooling-off period in clear business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear business days does the agreement give you to end it by written notice? 0 if it gives none.
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The public holidays in the Northern Territory in the weeks after the agreement was made (ISO 8601 dates).
      `the day I gave written notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the law practice written notice ending the agreement (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A `Cooling-off answer`
`s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` `the day the agreement was made` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `the public holidays` `the day I gave written notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` `the day the agreement was made` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `the public holidays`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 318(6) does not apply: the agreement gives no cooling-off period (it fails s 318(3)(e) unless you are a sophisticated client)`
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN
        IF `the day I gave written notice` `falls before` `the day the agreement was made`
        THEN `s 318(6) does not apply: the notice is dated before the agreement was made`
        ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the cooling-off period` (`the days from` `the day the agreement was made` `to` `the last day`)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the client` `give written notice terminating the conditional costs agreement` (`the days from` `the day the agreement was made` `to` `the day I gave written notice`)), (EVENT `the law practice` `recover the uplift fee` (`the days from` `the day the agreement was made` `to` `the day I gave written notice`)))
             WHEN FULFILLED THEN `s 318(6) does not apply: your notice came after the cooling-off period ended (the text's no)`
             OTHERWISE `No: you ended the agreement within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee (s 318(6)(b))`

-- s 318(6)(a): after termination within the cooling-off period the law practice "may recover only those legal costs in
-- respect of legal services performed for the client before that termination that were performed on the instructions
-- of the client and with the client's knowledge that the legal services would be performed during that period".
-- "only": FALSE where a condition fails. Outside s 318(6) (no termination within the period) NOTHING (NOTHING-kind).
@export Under s 318(6)(a) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), after I ended my conditional costs agreement within the cooling-off period, may the law practice recover its costs for a particular piece of work? NOTHING if you did not end it within the cooling-off period.
GIVEN `I ended it by written notice within the cooling-off period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you end the conditional costs agreement by written notice within its cooling-off period?
      `the work was done before I ended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the piece of work done before you ended the agreement?
      `the work was done on my instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the work done on your instructions?
      `I knew the work would be done during the cooling-off period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the work would be done during the cooling-off period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(6)(a) -- may the law practice recover its costs for this work` `I ended it by written notice within the cooling-off period` `the work was done before I ended it` `the work was done on my instructions` `I knew the work would be done during the cooling-off period` MEANS
    IF NOT `I ended it by written notice within the cooling-off period`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `the work was done before I ended it`
               AND `the work was done on my instructions`
               AND `I knew the work would be done during the cooling-off period`)

§§ `Uplift fees (s 308, s 319)`

-- s 308(1) "If a costs agreement involves an uplift fee, the law practice must, before entering the agreement, disclose
-- to the client in writing: (a) the practice's usual fees; and (b) the uplift fee or basis of the calculation of the
-- uplift fee; and (c) reasons why the uplift fee is warranted." (2) "not required ... to a sophisticated client."
-- FALSE where there is no uplift fee (the "if" fails) or the client is sophisticated (the text's no).
@export Under s 308 of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), must the law practice tell me in writing, before I enter the costs agreement, its usual fees, the uplift fee (or how it is calculated) and why the uplift fee is warranted?
GIVEN `the agreement has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the costs agreement provide for an uplift fee: extra legal costs (beyond disbursements) payable if your matter succeeds?
      `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the clients listed in s 306(1)(c) (a lawyer or law practice, a public or large company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a large professional partnership, certain joint ventures, a council, a minister, department or public authority)? An individual claimant answers false.
      `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the legal costs, or the basis on which they will be calculated, agreed as a result of a tender process?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 308 -- must the law practice tell me about the uplift fee in writing before I sign` `the agreement has an uplift fee` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` MEANS
        `the agreement has an uplift fee`
    AND (NOT (`s 295 -- a sophisticated client` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process`))

-- s 319(4): the most uplift fee in a litigious matter: the prescribed percentage of the legal costs (excluding
-- disbursements) otherwise payable. NOTHING where the matter is not litigious: s 319(4) then sets no cap.
@export Under s 319(4) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), what is the most uplift fee my conditional costs agreement may provide for in a litigious matter? NOTHING if the matter is not litigious (s 319(4) then sets no cap).
GIVEN `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your matter involve, or is it likely to involve, proceedings being issued in a court or tribunal?
      `the legal costs otherwise payable, excluding disbursements` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs, in dollars and excluding disbursements, payable under the agreement apart from the uplift fee.
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) for s 319(4), as a number (25 for 25%). The regulations are not part of this encoding.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 319(4) -- the most uplift fee in a litigious matter` `my matter is litigious` `the legal costs otherwise payable, excluding disbursements` `the prescribed percentage` MEANS
    IF `my matter is litigious`
    THEN JUST ((`the legal costs otherwise payable, excluding disbursements` TIMES `the prescribed percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING

@export Under s 319 of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), which requirements for an uplift fee does my conditional costs agreement fail to meet? An empty list means none. Any failure makes the agreement void (s 322(1)) and the uplift fee irrecoverable (s 322(4)).
GIVEN `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the uplift fee include or apply to disbursements (outlays such as court fees or experts' fees)?
      `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement separately identify how the uplift fee is calculated?
      `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement specify an estimate of the uplift fee?
      `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: was a single estimate not reasonably practicable (as the costs assessor would find)?
      `a range of estimates is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: does the agreement specify a range of estimates of the uplift fee?
      `the major variables are explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: does the agreement explain the major variables that will affect the calculation of the uplift fee?
      `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your matter involve, or is it likely to involve, proceedings being issued in a court or tribunal?
      `the uplift fee as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee as a percentage of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable, as a number (25 for 25%).
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) for s 319(4), as a number (25 for 25%).
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 319 -- what my uplift fee fails to meet` `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` `a range of estimates is specified` `the major variables are explained` `my matter is litigious` `the uplift fee as a percentage` `the prescribed percentage` MEANS
    `s 319 -- contraventions` (`the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` `a range of estimates is specified` `the major variables are explained` `my matter is litigious` `the uplift fee as a percentage` `the prescribed percentage` FALSE FALSE)
    -- every field the s 319 rules do not read is a fixed placeholder

§§ `Contingency fees (s 320)`

-- s 320(1) "must not enter into" (a flat negative), (2) "does not apply to the extent ...".
@export Under s 320 of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), does the Act forbid my costs agreement because my lawyer's fee is calculated by reference to what I recover (an award, a settlement or the value of property)? TRUE means forbidden, and the law practice may then recover nothing and must repay what it received (s 322(5)).
GIVEN `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any part of the amount payable to the law practice calculated by reference to the amount of an award or settlement, or the value of property, that may be recovered in the proceedings (for example "30% of whatever you get")?
      `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that calculation only the agreement adopting an applicable fixed costs provision (a scale or determination fixing costs made under legislation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 320 -- does the Act forbid a fee based on what I recover` `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision` MEANS
    `s 320 -- prohibited` `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision`

§§ `Void costs agreements (s 321, s 322)`

@export Under s 322(1) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), which provisions of Division 5 (ss 317 to 320) does my costs agreement contravene? An empty list means none; any entry makes the agreement void.
GIVEN `how it was made` IS A `How the agreement was made` @desc How was your costs agreement made? One of: a written agreement; an oral agreement evidenced in writing; a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct; an oral agreement with nothing in writing.
      `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does it clearly say it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement? Answer true if not made by an offer.
      `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does it clearly say it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct? Answer true if not made by an offer.
      `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does it clearly say what conduct will count as acceptance? Answer true if not made by an offer.
      `it says my costs are not subject to costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that your legal costs are not subject to costs assessment?
      `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the clients listed in s 306(1)(c) (a lawyer or law practice, a public or large company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a large professional partnership, certain joint ventures, a council, a minister, department or public authority)? An individual claimant answers false.
      `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the legal costs, or the basis on which they will be calculated, agreed as a result of a tender process?
      `payment depends on a successful outcome` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement make payment of some or all of your legal costs conditional on a successful outcome of the matter ("no win, no fee")?
      `the kind of matter` IS A `The kind of matter` @desc What kind of matter is it? One of: criminal proceedings; proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth); proceedings prescribed by the regulations; any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim.
      `it sets out what counts as success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: does it set out the circumstances that count as a successful outcome?
      `it is in clear plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: is it in clear plain language?
      `I signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: did you sign it?
      `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: does it state that you were informed of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it?
      `the cooling-off period in clear business days` IS A NUMBER @desc If conditional: how many clear business days does it give you to end it by written notice? 0 if none.
      `it has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide for an uplift fee: extra legal costs payable if your matter succeeds?
      `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is an uplift fee: does it include or apply to disbursements?
      `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is an uplift fee: does the agreement separately identify how it is calculated?
      `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is an uplift fee: does the agreement specify an estimate of it?
      `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: was a single estimate not reasonably practicable?
      `a range of estimates is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: does the agreement specify a range of estimates?
      `the major variables are explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: does it explain the major variables affecting the uplift fee?
      `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your matter involve, or is it likely to involve, proceedings being issued in a court or tribunal?
      `the uplift fee as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee as a percentage of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable (25 for 25%); 0 if none.
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) for s 319(4) (25 for 25%).
      `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any part of the amount payable calculated by reference to an award, a settlement or the value of property recovered?
      `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that calculation only the agreement adopting an applicable fixed costs provision made under legislation?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 322(1) -- which provisions does my costs agreement contravene` `how it was made` `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` `it says my costs are not subject to costs assessment` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` `payment depends on a successful outcome` `the kind of matter` `it sets out what counts as success` `it is in clear plain language` `I signed it` `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `it has an uplift fee` `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` `a range of estimates is specified` `the major variables are explained` `my matter is litigious` `the uplift fee as a percentage` `the prescribed percentage` `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision` MEANS
    `s 322(1) -- the provisions contravened` (`the agreement` `how it was made` `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` `it says my costs are not subject to costs assessment` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` `payment depends on a successful outcome` `the kind of matter` `it sets out what counts as success` `it is in clear plain language` `I signed it` `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `it has an uplift fee` `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` `a range of estimates is specified` `the major variables are explained` `my matter is litigious` `the uplift fee as a percentage` `the prescribed percentage` `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision`)

@export Under s 322(1) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), is my costs agreement void? It is void if it contravenes any provision of Division 5 (ss 317 to 320); if not void, s 321 lets it be enforced like any other contract, subject to costs assessment.
GIVEN `how it was made` IS A `How the agreement was made` @desc How was your costs agreement made? One of: a written agreement; an oral agreement evidenced in writing; a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct; an oral agreement with nothing in writing.
      `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does it clearly say it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement? Answer true if not made by an offer.
      `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does it clearly say it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct? Answer true if not made by an offer.
      `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was a written offer: does it clearly say what conduct will count as acceptance? Answer true if not made by an offer.
      `it says my costs are not subject to costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that your legal costs are not subject to costs assessment?
      `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the clients listed in s 306(1)(c) (a lawyer or law practice, a public or large company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a large professional partnership, certain joint ventures, a council, a minister, department or public authority)? An individual claimant answers false.
      `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the legal costs, or the basis on which they will be calculated, agreed as a result of a tender process?
      `payment depends on a successful outcome` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement make payment of some or all of your legal costs conditional on a successful outcome of the matter ("no win, no fee")?
      `the kind of matter` IS A `The kind of matter` @desc What kind of matter is it? One of: criminal proceedings; proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth); proceedings prescribed by the regulations; any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim.
      `it sets out what counts as success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: does it set out the circumstances that count as a successful outcome?
      `it is in clear plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: is it in clear plain language?
      `I signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: did you sign it?
      `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If conditional: does it state that you were informed of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it?
      `the cooling-off period in clear business days` IS A NUMBER @desc If conditional: how many clear business days does it give you to end it by written notice? 0 if none.
      `it has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide for an uplift fee: extra legal costs payable if your matter succeeds?
      `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is an uplift fee: does it include or apply to disbursements?
      `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is an uplift fee: does the agreement separately identify how it is calculated?
      `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is an uplift fee: does the agreement specify an estimate of it?
      `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: was a single estimate not reasonably practicable?
      `a range of estimates is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: does the agreement specify a range of estimates?
      `the major variables are explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no estimate: does it explain the major variables affecting the uplift fee?
      `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your matter involve, or is it likely to involve, proceedings being issued in a court or tribunal?
      `the uplift fee as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee as a percentage of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable (25 for 25%); 0 if none.
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulations (NT) for s 319(4) (25 for 25%).
      `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any part of the amount payable calculated by reference to an award, a settlement or the value of property recovered?
      `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that calculation only the agreement adopting an applicable fixed costs provision made under legislation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 322(1) -- is my costs agreement void` `how it was made` `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` `it says my costs are not subject to costs assessment` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` `payment depends on a successful outcome` `the kind of matter` `it sets out what counts as success` `it is in clear plain language` `I signed it` `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `it has an uplift fee` `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` `a range of estimates is specified` `the major variables are explained` `my matter is litigious` `the uplift fee as a percentage` `the prescribed percentage` `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision` MEANS
    `s 322(1) -- void` (`the agreement` `how it was made` `the offer says it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement` `the offer says it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct` `the offer says what conduct will be acceptance` `it says my costs are not subject to costs assessment` `I am a client listed in s 306(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` `payment depends on a successful outcome` `the kind of matter` `it sets out what counts as success` `it is in clear plain language` `I signed it` `it states I was told of my right to independent advice` `the cooling-off period in clear business days` `it has an uplift fee` `the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements` `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified` `an estimate of the uplift fee is specified` `an estimate was not reasonably practicable` `a range of estimates is specified` `the major variables are explained` `my matter is litigious` `the uplift fee as a percentage` `the prescribed percentage` `the fee is calculated by reference to what I recover` `the agreement adopts an applicable fixed costs provision`)

-- s 322(2) to (6). The void agreement's reason matters only as: a s 320 contravention, a s 319 contravention, or any
-- other; the client states which of the facts apply through the same inputs as above, reduced to the three that decide
-- the amounts (the others are fixed so that the agreement is void for the stated reason).
DECLARE `Why my costs agreement is void` IS ONE OF
    `it is not void`
    `it charges a contingency fee contrary to s 320`
    `its uplift fee contravenes s 319`
    `it contravenes another provision of Division 5`

GIVEN `why` IS A `Why my costs agreement is void`
GIVETH A `Costs agreement facts`
`an agreement void because` `why` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `it is not void` THEN
        `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 25 FALSE FALSE
    WHEN `it charges a contingency fee contrary to s 320` THEN
        `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 25 TRUE FALSE
    WHEN `its uplift fee contravenes s 319` THEN
        `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 25 FALSE FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        `the agreement` `an oral agreement with nothing in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 25 FALSE FALSE

@export Under s 322(2) to (5) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), if my costs agreement is void, what is the most the law practice may recover from me? NOTHING if the agreement is not void (s 322 then does not apply).
GIVEN `why it is void` IS A `Why my costs agreement is void` @desc Why is the agreement void (see the question "which provisions does my costs agreement contravene")? One of: it is not void; it charges a contingency fee contrary to s 320; its uplift fee contravenes s 319; it contravenes another provision of Division 5. Where both s 320 and s 319 are contravened, choose s 320.
      `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the legal costs the agreement would have entitled the law practice to, apart from any uplift fee, had it not been void.
      `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the uplift fee the agreement would have entitled the law practice to, had it not been void (0 if none).
      `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the fair and reasonable value of the legal services provided, as found on a costs assessment (s 314(c), s 341).
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `why it is void` `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services` MEANS
    `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover` (`an agreement void because` `why it is void`) `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services`

@export Under s 322(3) to (6) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), if my costs agreement is void, how much must the law practice repay me? If it does not repay, you may recover the amount as a debt in a court (s 322(6)). NOTHING if the agreement is not void.
GIVEN `why it is void` IS A `Why my costs agreement is void` @desc Why is the agreement void? One of: it is not void; it charges a contingency fee contrary to s 320; its uplift fee contravenes s 319; it contravenes another provision of Division 5. Where both s 320 and s 319 are contravened, choose s 320.
      `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the legal costs the agreement would have entitled the law practice to, apart from any uplift fee, had it not been void.
      `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the uplift fee the agreement would have entitled the law practice to, had it not been void (0 if none).
      `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the fair and reasonable value of the legal services provided, as found on a costs assessment.
      `the amount I have paid` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: everything you have paid the law practice for its legal services in the matter, including any uplift fee.
      `the part of it paid as uplift fee` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the part of what you paid that was in respect of the uplift fee (0 if none).
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `why it is void` `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services` `the amount I have paid` `the part of it paid as uplift fee` MEANS
    `s 322 -- what the law practice must repay` (`an agreement void because` `why it is void`) `the costs the agreement would have given, without uplift` `the uplift fee the agreement would have given` `the fair and reasonable value of the legal services` `the amount I have paid` `the part of it paid as uplift fee`

§§ `Disputing costs under the agreement (s 323, s 339, s 352) -- only if you dispute the costs`

-- s 339(1): the costs assessor "must assess any disputed costs that are subject to a costs agreement by reference to the
-- provisions of the costs agreement if: (a) a relevant provision of the costs agreement specifies the amount, or a rate
-- or other means for calculating the amount, of the costs; and (b) the agreement has not been set aside under section
-- 323; unless the assessor is satisfied: (c) the agreement does not comply in a material respect with any disclosure
-- requirements of Division 3; or (d) Division 5 precludes the law practice concerned from recovering the amount of the
-- costs; or (e) the parties otherwise agree." "if ... unless": FALSE when (a) or (b) fails or an "unless" limb is met
-- (fork F8 for the "unless").
@export Under s 339 of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), on a costs assessment, must the costs assessor assess my disputed costs by the amounts or rates in my costs agreement?
GIVEN `the agreement specifies the amount or a rate for these costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of your costs agreement specify the amount of the disputed costs, or a rate or other means for calculating it?
      `the agreement has been set aside under s 323` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a costs assessor set the agreement aside under s 323?
      `the assessor is satisfied the disclosure was materially deficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the costs assessor satisfied that the agreement does not comply in a material respect with the disclosure requirements of Division 3 (ss 303 to 313)?
      `the assessor is satisfied Division 5 stops the practice recovering these costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the costs assessor satisfied that Division 5 (for example a void agreement under s 322) precludes the law practice from recovering the amount?
      `the law practice and I have agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and the law practice agreed that the costs should not be assessed by reference to the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` `the agreement specifies the amount or a rate for these costs` `the agreement has been set aside under s 323` `the assessor is satisfied the disclosure was materially deficient` `the assessor is satisfied Division 5 stops the practice recovering these costs` `the law practice and I have agreed otherwise` MEANS
        `the agreement specifies the amount or a rate for these costs`
    AND (NOT `the agreement has been set aside under s 323`)
    AND (NOT (    `the assessor is satisfied the disclosure was materially deficient`
              OR  `the assessor is satisfied Division 5 stops the practice recovering these costs`
              OR  `the law practice and I have agreed otherwise`))

DECLARE `Set-aside answer` IS ONE OF
    `Yes: on your application, the costs assessor may order the costs agreement set aside, and must then fix the fair and reasonable costs (s 323(1), (4), (5))`
    `No: the costs assessor is not satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable, so s 323(1) gives no order (the text's no)`
    `s 323 does not give you an application: you are not a client of the law practice nor an associated third party payer who made the agreement without the client`

-- s 323(1) "On application by a client, the costs assessor may order that a costs agreement be set aside if satisfied
-- the agreement is not fair or reasonable." (11) "client means a person to whom or for whom legal services are or have
-- been provided." s 317(6): for an agreement between the law practice and an associated third party payer to which the
-- client is not a party, "client" in s 323 means the associated third party payer. s 311(3): a failure to disclose
-- also lets the client apply under s 323 -- the application is the same; the failure is one of the s 323(2) matters.
-- The assessor's satisfaction is an input; the order stays a discretion ("may").
@export Under s 323 of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), can my costs agreement be set aside? Yes if you apply and the costs assessor is satisfied it is not fair or reasonable (the order remains the assessor's discretion).
GIVEN `legal services are or were provided to me or for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are (or were) the law practice's legal services provided to you or for you?
      `I am an associated third party payer who made the agreement without the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: are you an associated third party payer (owing the law practice payment of the client's costs) who made the costs agreement with the law practice, with the client not a party to it?
      `the costs assessor is satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the costs assessor satisfied that the agreement is not fair or reasonable (having regard to such things as fraud or misrepresentation, a failure to make the required disclosures, and the parties' conduct before and after it was made, s 323(2))?
GIVETH A `Set-aside answer`
`s 323 -- can my costs agreement be set aside` `legal services are or were provided to me or for me` `I am an associated third party payer who made the agreement without the client` `the costs assessor is satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `legal services are or were provided to me or for me`) AND (NOT `I am an associated third party payer who made the agreement without the client`)
    THEN `s 323 does not give you an application: you are not a client of the law practice nor an associated third party payer who made the agreement without the client`
    ELSE IF `the costs assessor is satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable`
         THEN `Yes: on your application, the costs assessor may order the costs agreement set aside, and must then fix the fair and reasonable costs (s 323(1), (4), (5))`
         ELSE `No: the costs assessor is not satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable, so s 323(1) gives no order (the text's no)`

-- s 323(5), (6): on setting aside, the assessor "must determine the fair and reasonable legal costs in relation to the
-- work to which the agreement related" but "may not order the payment of an amount in excess of the amount that the
-- law practice would have been entitled to recover if the costs agreement had not been set aside".
@export Under s 323(5) and (6) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), if my costs agreement is set aside, what is the most the costs assessor may order me to pay? The fair and reasonable costs the assessor determines, but never more than the agreement would have given.
GIVEN `the fair and reasonable costs the assessor determines` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the fair and reasonable legal costs for the work, as the costs assessor determines them under s 323(5).
      `what the agreement would have given the law practice` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: what the law practice would have been entitled to recover under the agreement had it not been set aside (including any uplift fee).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 323(6) -- the most I can be ordered to pay after a set-aside` `the fair and reasonable costs the assessor determines` `what the agreement would have given the law practice` MEANS
    min `the fair and reasonable costs the assessor determines` `what the agreement would have given the law practice`

DECLARE `Review time answer` IS ONE OF
    `In time: within 28 days after the s 323 determination (s 352(2)(a)(i))`
    `Out of time unless the reviewer allows further time (s 352(2)(a))`
    `The determination has not yet been made on that day`

-- s 352(1)(a), (2)(a)(i): run as the regulative rule `the time to apply for review of a set-aside determination`.
@export Under s 352(2)(a) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), am I in time to apply to a reviewer for review of a costs assessor's order or determination under s 323 about my costs agreement? The application must be made within 28 days after the determination is made, unless the reviewer allows further time.
GIVEN `the day the determination was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the costs assessor made the order or determination under s 323 (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-11-06).
      `the day I apply for review` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the application for review (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A `Review time answer`
`s 352(2)(a) -- am I in time to seek review of a set-aside determination` `the day the determination was made` `the day I apply for review` MEANS
    IF `the day I apply for review` `falls before` `the day the determination was made`
    THEN `The determination has not yet been made on that day`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the time to apply for review of a set-aside determination` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the client` `apply to a reviewer for review of the s 323 determination` (`the days from` `the day the determination was made` `to` `the day I apply for review`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `In time: within 28 days after the s 323 determination (s 352(2)(a)(i))`
         OTHERWISE `Out of time unless the reviewer allows further time (s 352(2)(a))`

@export Under s 352(2)(a) of the Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), what is the last day to apply for review of a costs assessor's s 323 order or determination about my costs agreement (unless the reviewer allows further time)?
GIVEN `the day the determination was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the costs assessor made the order or determination under s 323 (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A DATE
`s 352(2)(a) -- the last day to seek review of a set-aside determination` `the day the determination was made` MEANS
    `the day the determination was made` `plus` 28 `days`
